# CQ 07: Which states enter an operator, and which leave it?
# process operator?
#
# Part 1, Figure 2 shows the transformation principle: an operator turns a
# status ante into a status post. Both are sets of products, energies and
# information, and the standard does not pair an individual input with an
# individual output. Asking which input becomes which output therefore has no
# answer in VDI 3682, and a query joining hasInput with hasOutput would return
# their cartesian product, which reads as a pairing that was never asserted.
#
# The query reports the two sets separately, one row per operator, which is
# what the standard does state.
PREFIX vdi3682: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#>
SELECT ?operator
       (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?ante; separator=", ") AS ?statusAnte)
       (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?post; separator=", ") AS ?statusPost)
WHERE {
  ?operator a vdi3682:ProcessOperator .
  OPTIONAL { ?operator vdi3682:hasInput  ?ante }
  OPTIONAL { ?operator vdi3682:hasOutput ?post }
} GROUP BY ?operator ORDER BY ?operator
